@TicketMaintenance.API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5135

### Health check (anonymous)
GET {{TicketMaintenance.API_HostAddress}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

### Login (anonymous, rate-limited to 10/min) -> save the token
# @name login
POST {{TicketMaintenance.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo.operator@example.com",
  "password": "demo1234"
}

###

@authToken = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Current account (requires token)
GET {{TicketMaintenance.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### Update profile: name/email, optional password change (requires token)
PUT {{TicketMaintenance.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Demo Operator",
  "email": "demo.operator@example.com"
}

###

### List tickets without a token -> 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{TicketMaintenance.API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets?limit=50

###

### Lookups (requires token)
GET {{TicketMaintenance.API_HostAddress}}/api/lookups
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### Create ticket (the token identifies the creator; no actor field in the body)
POST {{TicketMaintenance.API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "ATM-0451 out of service",
  "description": "Screen not responding",
  "priorityId": 3,
  "categoryId": 1
}

###

### Assign operator (the token identifies the actor; operator must have OPERATOR role)
# POST {{TicketMaintenance.API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/1/assign
# Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# {
#   "operatorId": 2
# }

###
